    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nI found that after typing a specific Thai character \"ำ\" the typing messes up badly.\nThis only affects the rendition.\nI confirm that it persists across different terminal emulators and downgrading to version 0.10.4 solves the problem.\nPlease see the attached video. \n[Video demo](https://youtu.be/zCjdo5IqgIk)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nType ำ and anything that follows it will not show correctly.\nYou could try copy the above character and then type anything even in English.\n\nFor instance, you could \n1. copy `จำ` and paste into neovim.\n2. type `here` after.\nWhat I see is that `h` disappears as soon as the next `e` is typed.\nIf you insert a new line, the rendition is also off.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nText laid out correctly character by character.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.11\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nFedora 42\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nAlacritty 0.15.1 / Kitty 0.41.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\ndnf",
